I've been playing Nethack for a little over a year, since May 2004.
I've exclusively played barbarians, figuring that if I couldn't ascend
with a class often considered to be the easiest, then it would be
hopeless to attempt the rest. I actually started out by playing about
five knights in a row, but this novice found the rules for knights a
bit restrictive, so I switched to barbarians. (I also savescummed my
way to an 'ascension' last summer, but I was so ashamed and the
experience was so unrewarding, I vowed I would never savescum again :-)
If a titan destroys you on Medusa's Island, or an eel drowns you in the
Castle moat, well then, that's it!)

The game which would eventually become my first ascension actually
began on 12-30-2004. I played it off and on over the next few weeks,
but stopped in February when I was finally ready for the ascension run,
because I was so scared of screwing it up. Finally, last night, I
completed it in a few hours.

A few notes. 'Beren Belagund' is a splicing together of two names I
loved from Tolkien's _Silmarillion_. Yes, I used up 10 wishes, which is
embarrassing, but come on, I had to ascend! Also, h ; L R P T were
genocided, which is a bit of an overkill (especially the last two).
I've found that Mjollnir and silver saber are an excellent combination
for a barbarian.

I was terribly afraid of being burdened on the Astral Plane. I
jettisoned *everything*: all my gold and gems, and most of my food,
scrolls, rings, and wands. And yet I was *still* burdened, probably due
to, uh, my 49 potions of full healing and my 28 potions of holy water
(can anyone say, "obsesssed with avoiding hitpoint drain on the Plane
of Air"? :-) However, I calculated that I could ditch 16 potions of
holy water upon entering Astral, and shed the 'burdened' state, and
that is exactly what happened.

It says I killed Death twice, but it must have been indirectly via the
conflict intrinsic, since I never faced him. Indeed, I never faced any
of the Riders; just did a quick dash off to the left-hand temple, by
zapping a few pathways open via wand of teleportation, and happened to
pick the right one. I was so nervous that I dropped the Amulet on the
altar thinking that was the way to sacrifice it :-)

I don't recall much about the pre-ascension game back in Dec-Feb,
except that I wished for a blessed figurine of an Archon, only to have
my brand new pet swallowed by a purple worm somewhere near the Valley
of the Dead. Bummer.

Googling this group's archives has been an invaluable resource. Thanks
you all.

